      "writtenOn": "2023-07-22T18:26:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After thinking about this more, the RGBA-\u003eYUVA step could also be externalized to a utility built on top of the Skia API. The Graphite version up to the point where the transfers are done is basically the public API implementation. \n\nPerhaps, if this were all being rethought from a clean slate, the only thing that Graphite/Ganesh should provide is a way to async read multiple images with one callback, as a convenience for YUV[A]. Even that is not really necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "d8b4d845_1e31f44c",
      "revId": "0a17544e891f7a3f299be42d0414e1a8c53728f0",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
